{
  "page_id": "EM-30",
  "section_header": "ENGINE MECHANICAL — Cylinder Head",
  "title": "REMOVE CAMSHAFTS FROM CAMSHAFT HOUSINGS AND INSPECT",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 1,
      "description": "Illustration showing hands removing camshaft from housing by turning it",
      "labels": [
        "EM042"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 3,
        "left": 3,
        "width": 40,
        "height": 28
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "2. REMOVE CAMSHAFTS FROM CAMSHAFT HOUSINGS"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "(a) Remove camshaft housing rear covers by loosening the bolts.",
        "(b) While turning the camshaft, slowly pull it out so as not to damage the camshaft housing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 2,
      "description": "Illustration showing hands using a micrometer to measure camshaft lobe height",
      "labels": [],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 32,
        "left": 3,
        "width": 40,
        "height": 23
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "3. INSPECT CAMSHAFTS AND CAMSHAFT HOUSINGS"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "(a) Using a micrometer, measure the cam lobes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Standard lobe height"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "caption": "Standard lobe height",
      "headers": [
        "Type",
        "Specification"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Intake",
          "35.660 – 35.670 mm (1.4039 – 1.0043 in.)"
        ],
        [
          "Exhaust",
          "35.662 – 35.672 mm (1.0040 – 1.0044 in.)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Minimum lobe height"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "caption": "Minimum lobe height",
      "headers": [
        "Type",
        "Specification"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Intake",
          "35.465 mm (1.3963 in.)"
        ],
        [
          "Exhaust",
          "35.467 mm (1.3968 in.)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If the lobe height is less than the minimum allowable, the camshaft is worn and must be replaced."
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 3,
      "description": "Illustration showing camshaft placed on V-blocks with dial indicator measuring runout at center journal",
      "labels": [
        "EM031"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 56,
        "left": 3,
        "width": 40,
        "height": 23
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "(b) Place the camshaft on V-blocks and measure the runout at the center journal."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Maximum circle runout: 0.04 mm (0.0016 in.)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If the runout is greater than maximum allowable, replace the camshaft."
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 4,
      "description": "Illustration showing hands using a micrometer to measure camshaft journal diameter",
      "labels": [
        "EM032"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 80,
        "left": 3,
        "width": 40,
        "height": 17
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "(c) Using a micrometer, measure the journal diameter."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Standard journal diameter:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "caption": "Standard journal diameter",
      "headers": [
        "Journal No.",
        "Specification"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "No. 1",
          "37.959 – 37.975 mm (1.4944 – 1.4951 in.)"
        ],
        [
          "No. 2",
          "42.959 – 42.975 mm (1.6913 – 1.6919 in.)"
        ],
        [
          "No. 3",
          "43.459 – 43.475 mm (1.7110 – 1.7116 in.)"
        ],
        [
          "No. 4",
          "43.959 – 43.975 mm (1.7307 – 1.7313 in.)"
        ],
        [
          "No. 5",
          "44.459 – 44.475 mm (1.7504 – 1.7510 in.)"
        ],
        [
          "No. 6",
          "44.959 – 44.975 mm (1.7700 – 1.7707 in.)"
        ],
        [
          "No. 7",
          "45.459 – 45.475 mm (1.7897 – 1.7904 in.)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "diagram",
      "index": 5,
      "description": "Illustration showing hands using an inside micrometer to measure camshaft housing bore",
      "labels": [
        "EM013"
      ],
      "bbox": {
        "top": 97,
        "left": 3,
        "width": 40,
        "height": 15
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "(d) Using an inside micrometer, measure the housing bore."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "(e) Subtract the journal diameter measurement from the housing bore measurement."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Standard clearance: 0.025 – 0.066 mm (0.0010 – 0.0026 in.)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Maximum clearance: 0.1 mm (0.004 in.)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If the clearance is greater than maximum, replace the camshaft and if necessary, the housing."
    }
  ]
}
